<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21249" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĭacchus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴακχος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A poetic and mystical appellation of Bacchus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				E. 7, 61</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. G. 1, 166</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Leg.
				2, 14, 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cat. 64, 251</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4,
			15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b> transf., like Bacchus, <i>wine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(Silenum) Inflatum hesterno venas, ut semper,
					Iaccho,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 6, 15</span></i>
			: multo madefactus, Col. poët. 10, 309.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
